WEBVTT

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:34.990
We've arrived.

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:36.740
Shamon-sama is waiting for us.

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:41.870
This way.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:44.750
Come in quietly.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:03.810
Shamon-sama!

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:05.180
Would you wake up?!

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:06.600
You have guests.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.020
Ow-ow-ow-ow.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:11.610
Sorry, sorry.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:13.610
I was so absorbed in my training

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:16.530
that I must have achieved
a state of enlightenment.

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:19.160
Maybe you just drank too much?

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:24.290
Oh!

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:25.750
So this is the one.

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:27.960
The kid you were talking about.

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:30.000
He reeks of booze!

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.460
It reminds me of that time two years ago.

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:34.710
My name is Shamon.

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:35.960
Nice to meet you, kid.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:39.220
Welcome, my mysterious guest.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:46.810
Right.

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:49.190
Kuchiha, give me what you've grated.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.560
That certainly smells good.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:55.980
Well, you've got my attention.

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:57.990
I'll listen to your story.

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:01.780
Clam rice and fermented soybean soup.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:03.990
Fried white radish on the side.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:06.700
This should be an ample meal.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.330
Eat it all and don't leave anything.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:16.630
How is it? Good?

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:18.630
Yes, very.

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:23.300
However, the more I hear of your story,
the less I want to believe it.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:27.930
I sensed a strong, unearthly spirit
when I was in town, so I went after it.

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:30.690
When I got there, the Nue
was already attacking him.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:34.860
It's a rare thing for a Nue to attack someone.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:38.730
Before that monster attacked me, I was normal.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:42.570
This reminds me of when I met Kon.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:45.780
That is to say...

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:48.950
Toki, you're like Kon, aren't you?

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:50.960
You're from another world.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:53.080
Is that about right?

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:54.830
Yes.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.840
So I suppose you're looking
for a way to go home.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:03.050
I guess.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:05.970
I'm sorry to tell you this,
since you came here for my help,

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:08.430
but I'll tell you plainly. It's impossible.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:16.520
Kon's still here because I have no idea
how to send him back either.

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:18.070
However...

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.780
we <i>do</i> have a few things to work with.

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:24.490
We know that when Kon got here, the Nue attacked him too.

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:28.620
I'm certain that the Nue and Yakou
hold the keys to this.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:34.170
They only appear rarely,
and they're strange spirits,

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:36.630
but we have nothing to lose
by trying to catch them.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:41.300
Well, as soon as I get any useful information, I'll let you know.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:43.090
You can leave that much to me.

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:46.430
You should stay at this temple until you get used to things.

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:51.180
I have a lot of influence around here, and I'd feel more at ease that way.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:52.810
Ah, sure.

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:54.350
Thank you very much.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:58.110
Kon, Kuchiha, look after Tokidoki, okay?

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:00.110
Okay.

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:00.820
Um...

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:01.570
Yes?

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:02.400
Excuse me.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:05.110
Normal people can't see spirits, can they?

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:07.320
Then is information likely to reach you?

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:09.830
Sure it will.

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:14.080
After all, exterminating spirits is my job.

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:20.670
May I join you?

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:22.880
Sure.

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:30.220
So how does it feel to find out
that you're stuck here?

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:32.890
I don't really mind.

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:35.890
You're still damn calm about it.

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:37.810
It's the opposite.

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:40.150
I have no idea what's going on.

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:45.400
I was thinking I should concentrate on what I can actually do right now.

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:46.900
For example?

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:49.660
Helping with the housework and stuff.

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:54.080
You're a realist, aren't you?

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:58.870
There isn't much else I can help Shamon-san with, after all.

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:04.880
Even I know that looking after
a stranger like me is...

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:08.880
The monk is experienced
at being accommodating.

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:11.970
He took care of Kuchiha and me.

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:15.140
Like you, I was a stranger,

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:19.650
and Kuchiha has grown up with her own unique set of problems.

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:21.110
What do you mean?

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:24.730
She was born with a special condition.

00:06:24.730 --> 00:06:27.150
The monk accepted that and looked after her.

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:30.160
Even though it's in his job description,

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:33.830
he doesn't think of it as a burden.

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:36.160
Well, don't worry about it too much.

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:52.390
A dog?

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:55.890
Did I just imagine that?

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:03.230
Who was it?

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:05.650
Who the hell hung these here?

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:07.900
It must have been her.

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:14.370
Hey, you! Obstructing Kein-sama's path with laundry deserves punishment.

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:18.370
Hey, she's got a sword,
even though she's only a girl.

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:20.000
She's got some nerve.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:21.330
Hey, woman.

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:23.380
Who the hell do you think you are?

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:27.920
Samurai, I humbly offer my apologies.

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:30.510
Please—

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:31.970
Kuchiha!

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:36.100
Please have mercy.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:38.470
All right, I see.

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:41.060
Show me your face.

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:45.770
You have a surprisingly refined face, don't you?

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:46.980
Stop it!

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:49.360
What?

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:54.490
You're the ones who walked
into the temple grounds uninvited!

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:55.700
You! Stop it!

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:57.450
You bastard.

00:07:57.990 --> 00:07:59.660
You insolent fool!

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:02.040
What's with those fists?

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:03.750
Are you a barbarian?

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:08.840
Are you related to barbarians in some way?

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:09.960
This is perfect.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:12.050
I had this sharpened just yesterday.

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:14.430
This will be a fine chance to test
the edge on the blade.

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:16.680
Sh-Sharpened?

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:18.060
A sword?

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:21.390
Samurai-sama, if you must
attack someone, attack me.

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:23.060
Piss off. You're in the way.

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:27.020
Kuchiha!

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:30.190
Look for an opening,
and run back to the temple.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:31.320
But why?

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:33.780
At least look after your own life.

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:37.030
If you incur their wrath,
your life is as good as over.

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:38.280
No way.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:40.290
What are you muttering about over there?

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:45.040
Your opponent is over here.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:47.210
Those look good.

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:48.130
It's in the way.

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:49.000
I'll take it off.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:51.260
Yes, yes, take it off.

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:53.840
Let's see if that's really a woman.

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:54.630
Stop it!

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:59.970
Right, kid. Now we can test
the blade's sharpness.

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:02.350
Wa— St—

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:04.440
Stop!

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:13.320
Aren't you quite the courageous,
honorable samurai.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:14.530
What the hell?

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:17.240
You want to be killed?

00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:21.160
If you think you can strike me, then try.

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:25.370
If you want to bathe in my blood so much.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:29.500
In this inugami-tsuki blood.

00:09:30.590 --> 00:09:31.800
It's the mark of evil!

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:36.470
Shit! Let's get out of here!

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:37.550
We'll be cursed!

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:52.230
Kuchiha, are you okay?

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:53.400
Are you hurt?

00:09:55.690 --> 00:10:00.410
When our eyes met, you should have realized that I was pretending not to know you.

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:05.960
You're ten years too early to be thinking you can rescue me!

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:08.920
Why didn't you run like I told you?!

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:14.960
B-But if I see a girl in a dangerous situation,
I can't just leave her!

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:17.680
If you get hurt, then it'll be a problem for me!

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:23.720
Besides, I'm used to stuff like that.

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:30.100
They all ran off terrified.

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:32.730
What are inugami-tsuki anyway?

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:36.240
They are creatures so detested

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:39.530
that if outsiders found out about them,

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:42.740
this house would be reduced
to rubble in three days.

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:47.370
Th-Then, if we don't do something,
Kuchiha will—

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:50.330
Are you aware that in this era,

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:54.380
the penalties for fighting over
personal grievances are harsh?

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:58.470
It's not unusual for all those involved
to be put to death.

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:01.390
Knowing all that, do you still want to do something about it?

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:07.220
You just... piss me off.

00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:12.190
I <i>do</i> want to do something.

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:13.860
It may be selfish,

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:15.940
but I just won't feel right
unless I do something about it!

00:11:15.940 --> 00:11:19.150
Then what do you think we should do?

00:11:22.870 --> 00:11:24.280
Shinonome.

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:28.750
I guess there's no way to control the spirits here, is there?

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:30.830
I guess there isn't.

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:35.880
Then maybe I've just thought
of something I can do.

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:36.920
Oh?

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:40.670
Right. Let's get some payback.

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:51.480
Hey, watchman, wake up.

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:55.440
How many times do I have to tell you?

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:59.690
Stop loitering about the streets
until the dead of night!

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:04.620
Now, Heihachi.

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:07.160
That was a shitty welcome. Thank you.

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:10.200
Now you can work to pay me
back for the lantern.

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:11.580
Y-You bastard!

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:13.420
You did that on purpose!

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:15.250
You're not even welcome here!

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:16.630
You're too noisy.

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:17.920
You'll bother the neighbors.

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:19.340
And whose fault is that?! Whose?!

00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:20.550
Who knows?

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:21.220
Wha—

00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:25.180
So, Kon, are you plotting mischief again?

00:12:25.180 --> 00:12:29.390
I suppose so, but this time
I'm not doing it, he is.

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:33.980
Hi.

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:36.860
Is he a forei—

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:40.280
Um, I'm Toki.

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:42.700
It may not look like it, but I was born and raised in Japan.

00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:44.740
Nice to meet you, Heihachi-san.

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:46.120
Nice to meet you.

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:46.950
Let's go.

00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:50.950
So you're not living at the temple?

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:54.160
Kuchiha watches me all the time
when I'm there.

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:55.920
I'm more comfortable here.

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:58.090
Hey, take a seat.

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:05.930
I'll be in this place for a few days, I guess.

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:07.760
This is everything.

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:09.180
Think you can get it ready?

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:11.390
Sure, leave it to me.

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:13.930
Then I'll see you tomorrow evening.

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:19.150
Now, we need to teach you to use a still.

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:23.110
Why is something like this here in this era?

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:28.280
You know, they have cameras
and telescopes in this era.

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:31.450
You know a lot about science.

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:33.450
I'm surprised you've come to believe in spirits.

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:37.000
That's where you misunderstand.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:39.460
Is there a rabbit living on the moon?

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:41.170
No.

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:44.470
We know that there's no rabbit living there.

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:47.590
But this era doesn't have a space shuttle,

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:50.470
so they can't prove there's no rabbit making rice cakes up there.

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:54.480
Our way of thinking is based on science,

00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:57.480
but theirs is based on superstition.

00:13:57.480 --> 00:14:00.020
If you believe in gods, demons, and monsters,

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:02.980
then they really exist.

00:14:02.980 --> 00:14:05.990
I don't deny that way of thinking.

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:10.950
Well, all that's left is to let it ferment,

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:14.500
and then you can have
what you want, lead actor.

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:20.710
Kuchiha, are those two coming by today?

00:14:20.710 --> 00:14:23.500
I haven't seen them yet.

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:26.010
Kuchiha!

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:27.260
Your face...

00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:28.720
It's nothing.

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:31.720
I was careless and
bumped into something.

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:33.720
Seriously.

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:36.230
A girl should take better care of her face.

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:39.100
You bruised it by mistake?

00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:42.730
Be more careful.

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:45.610
Yes!

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:47.280
I'm really sorry.

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:51.160
Monster! I will destroy you!

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:55.290
And then, when I said that,
it turned and fled!

00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:59.330
So what is an inugami-tsuki exactly?

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:02.330
You don't know?

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:05.630
Well, I'm not educated.

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:08.130
Then I'll tell you.

00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:13.050
A kemono-tsuki is one that has a cursed symbol on its flesh,

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:17.890
a ferocious and dangerous creature that delights in slaughter.

00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:20.890
Th-There's a monster like that around here?

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:23.650
I saw it, right near here.

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:26.730
It must have escaped after
the monk captured it, I bet.

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:29.900
If I see it again, I'll fight and slay it!

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:33.410
Just like a valiant samurai.

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:41.120
Um, I have to say, samurai-sama,
that the bill is...

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:46.300
Hey, old man, you want money from me?!

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:50.220
But...

00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:57.470
Hey. What's that?

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:01.390
Bastard, are you listening to me, old man?

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:02.060
Why are you—

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:09.570
What the hell are you?

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:12.070
I am one who lives in that temple.

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:14.280
What are you talking about?

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:15.660
Stay away!

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:19.160
Old man...

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:21.250
Wh-What?

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:22.920
Hey, wait!

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:26.130
Wait! Don't leave me here!

00:16:29.710 --> 00:16:32.470
Be ashamed of your folly.

00:16:32.930 --> 00:16:36.300
You use your power to oppress others.

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:38.970
And now the same is inflicted upon you.

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:44.980
This is what you have done to others.

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:46.940
You and your comrades.

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:53.900
The next time, you won't
be let off with a threat.

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:56.160
Prepare yourself.

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:20.220
Well, well.

00:17:23.020 --> 00:17:24.430
H-Hot!

00:17:24.430 --> 00:17:25.980
It's hot!

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:28.480
Good work.

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:31.980
You guys! That was reckless.

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:33.320
You never told me about that!

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:35.610
About all the fire!

00:17:35.610 --> 00:17:38.870
It's all right. Everything's okay.

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:41.330
Good work, old man.

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:46.870
That guy ate for free every day.

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:49.330
Man, that felt good.

00:17:50.210 --> 00:17:53.630
So how did the trick work?

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:55.970
I knew who you were,
but I was still frightened.

00:17:55.970 --> 00:17:59.220
This liquid is made from potatoes.

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:01.930
It's called ethanol, and it burns pretty well.

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:04.980
If you soak your hand in water first

00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:07.640
and then put on the ethanol,

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:12.860
you can light a fire, and it won't feel hot because of the water.

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:15.900
It only lasts for a little while though.

00:18:17.360 --> 00:18:19.780
The lettering was done with tobacco ashes.

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:22.740
We burned tobacco weed until it turned white.

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:25.250
We mixed it with water and wrote the words.

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:29.170
That's supposed to make it more flammable,

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:32.000
so the flames only burned one part,

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:34.920
but...

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:37.300
I guess I won't be able to use it for a while.

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:39.680
We'll fix it right up for you.

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:41.140
Then that's fine.

00:18:41.140 --> 00:18:43.510
It's nothing serious.

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:45.850
I'm sorry.

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:48.810
You'll catch a cold.

00:18:50.270 --> 00:18:51.360
Thank you.

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:58.820
You're unexpectedly interesting.
I'll have to reconsider my opinion of you.

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:02.740
But if Shinonome hadn't made
the ingredients for me,

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:04.280
I couldn't have done it.

00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:08.460
You know, having the knowledge
is pretty amazing,

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:12.500
but actually putting the plan
into action is even more amazing.

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:15.750
Hey, what are you insinuating?

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:17.380
What indeed?

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:21.510
Giving the hard jobs to other people
isn't particularly impressive.

00:19:22.590 --> 00:19:24.930
That's rich coming from a guy who's good for nothing else.

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:26.720
What are you talking about?!

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:28.270
It's the truth, you joker.

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:29.560
Don't call me a joker!

00:19:30.810 --> 00:19:33.020
Hey, are you listening to me?

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:36.020
Our friend is laid up in bed because of this!

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:39.150
Is it your job to shelter demons?

00:19:39.150 --> 00:19:40.610
Well?

00:19:40.610 --> 00:19:41.860
Should we make you retire?
Now what?

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:42.700
Should we make you retire?

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:46.240
Or are you going to do it for us?

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:53.880
Those guys barged in, saying they were attacked by a demon last night.

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:57.880
They've been shouting complaints
at him non-stop.

00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:01.470
Are you satisfied, now that you've made problems for Shamon-sama too?

00:20:02.090 --> 00:20:03.970
What an idiotic thing to do!

00:20:05.050 --> 00:20:06.050
I'm sorry.

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:12.480
But... I couldn't believe you could get so used
to being harassed that you didn't mind.

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:17.770
I thought that even if you were used to it,
it must be hurting you, in your heart.

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:22.990
You fool.

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:34.080
You let emotion govern your actions too much,

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:36.250
and you cause trouble for those around you.

00:20:37.090 --> 00:20:39.420
Don't pull another stunt like that.

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:40.710
You can relax now.

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:43.180
And...

00:20:44.550 --> 00:20:45.680
Thank you.

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:52.180
Perhaps I <i>do</i> feel a little better.

00:20:56.230 --> 00:20:57.940
You're a noisy bunch.

00:20:57.940 --> 00:21:00.980
Do you think you could
leave sometime soon?

00:21:00.980 --> 00:21:04.740
We have no monsters, spirits,
or kemono-tsuki here.

00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:05.740
What?

00:21:06.030 --> 00:21:08.580
I'll tell you, because it looks
like you don't know.

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:13.000
I've been looking after this place for about ten years now,

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:16.500
and I've said this many times before.

00:21:16.880 --> 00:21:21.250
Those who delight in finding
other people's weaknesses,

00:21:21.250 --> 00:21:24.970
and in making themselves look
strong to oppress others,

00:21:24.970 --> 00:21:26.970
are the truly evil monsters!

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:31.010
Bastards... If you can understand that,
then get the hell <i>now</i>!

00:21:31.010 --> 00:21:33.020
You morons.

00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:43.240
Um, how long were you guys standing there?

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:44.360
Just for a little while.

00:21:44.360 --> 00:21:46.360
You know, you were pretty cool there.

00:21:46.360 --> 00:21:48.990
Man, that's embarrassing.
